---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs04.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 23"
    link="/germany/drs/drs23"
    linkText="View DRS 23"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 4, first issued in August 2000, was the DRSC's original standard elaborating capital consolidation and business combination accounting for group accounts – directly supplementing HGB §301's own capital consolidation mechanics, covered in detail in the earlier HGB poster series. It was last amended for BilMoG (2009) changes before its final withdrawal.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn – a fundamental rewrite, not a minor update</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn – a fundamental rewrite, not a minor update</div>
<div class="principle">Rather than incrementally amend DRS 4 again, the HGB-Fachausschuss undertook a GROUND-UP rewrite, addressing numerous practical issues DRS 4 had never resolved – including the mechanics of multi-tier ("mehrstufiger") group structures, given HGB's own conceptual model assumes a single-tier group as its baseline. The result, DRS 23 "Kapitalkonsolidierung (Einbeziehung von Tochterunternehmen in den Konzernabschluss)," was adopted 25 September 2015 and formally announced in the Bundesanzeiger on 23 February 2016, with DRS 4 withdrawn effective for fiscal years beginning after 31 December 2016.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Business combinations / capital consolidation in group accounts</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>First issued</span><span>August 2000</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Withdrawn</span><span>Effective for fiscal years beginning after 31.12.2016</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 23 – Kapitalkonsolidierung</strong> (ground-up rewrite, including multi-tier group mechanics)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
